{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KdNEaUJw3sRM78LGv24fJA","type":"tool_result","content":"diff --git a/.pose/specs/2026-11-26-pose-validate-read-only-index-followups.md b/.pose/specs/2026-11-26-pose-validate-read-only-index-followups.md\nindex 626a8ed2..9143e637 100644\n--- a/.pose/specs/2026-11-26-pose-validate-read-only-index-followups.md\n+++ b/.pose/specs/2026-11-26-pose-validate-read-only-index-followups.md\n@@ -107,7 +107,7 @@ The index is judged on the file actually opened, opened with `O_NONBLOCK` where\n \n ### Decision D3\n - Basis: R2\n-The index lookup runs under the caller's context where the caller has one (`ReadOnlyIndexContext`, used by the review history reader within its 30 s), and under a 30 s bound of its own otherwise. Git's standard error is kept, as its first line within 300 bytes, and a failure in which Git refuses the index (`index file …`, `bad signature`, `index uses … extension`, `bad index version`) is marked `ErrIndexUnreadable`; every read whose error is classified runs with `LC_ALL=C` (`GitEnglish`), so that holds in any locale. A failed lookup of the index is reported with Git's words and is not an index failure (no repository, a broken config or HEAD). The report stays silent only where the root is not a repository.\n+The index lookup runs under the caller's context where the caller has one (`ReadOnlyIndexContext`, used by the review history reader within its 30 s), and under a 30 s bound of its own otherwise. A failure is never classified from Git's words, which two rounds showed incomplete in both directions (a revision named after the index, index refusals worded otherwise, a warning printed first): scope selection resolves its revisions first and says \"revision unknown?\" only when one does not name a commit, and reports any other failure with all of Git's standard error, on one line within 600 bytes, read with `LC_ALL=C`. `ErrIndexUnreadable` marks only the read-only index's own failures. The report stays silent only where Git cannot open the repository at all, and states any other failure on one line without the checkout's absolute path.\n \n ## 6. Validation\n \n@@ -123,13 +123,14 @@ Each requirement gets a regression test shown failing before its code.\n - 2026-11-26: R1 opens without blocking and judges the opened file; R2 reports a failed index read in `check`, names it in scope selection (`ErrIndexUnreadable`) and warns in `report`; R3 locates the index with `--git-path` relative to the root, within a 30 s deadline; R4 falls back to the private copy when the memory file or its time cannot be set. Each has a test that fails with its guard mutated out: `TestReadOnlyIndexToleratesAnAtomicallyReplacedIndex`, `TestAFailedIndexReadIsReported`, `TestReadOnlyIndexFindsTheIndexFromASubdirectory`, `TestThePrivateIndexCopyLeavesTheIndexAlone`. R6 adds `TestReadOnlyIndexDiffCoversConflictsRangesAndDirtySubmodules`, which passes on the existing reader. R5 is L1 (D1).\n - 2026-11-26: review round 1 (rrn-4262ae59adfc1641) requested changes. N1–N2: a corrupt index, which Git itself refuses, is now reported with Git's own message and marked as an index failure in check, scope selection and report (`TestACorruptIndexIsReportedWithItsCause`; fails with the classification or check's capture removed). N3: D3. N4: the memfd and timestamp calls are replaceable, and `TestReadOnlyIndexFallsBackWithoutAMemoryFile` fails with either fallback removed. N5: the R6 test makes the stat cache stale before every read, so it fails with the protection or the ledger's use of it removed, and the CLI concurrency test runs `ReviewRunHistoryFindings`. N8: failures handing the index to Git are index failures, and a failing memfd write falls back too. N9: the report states that the list could not be read, and a plain `pose report` outside a repository stays silent. N10: the check's findings are localised. N6, N7 and N11 are follow-ups.\n - 2026-11-26: review round 2 (rrn-ef7133259b2c911e) requested changes. N12: the plain `report` listing runs in English and is silent only outside a repository (`reportChangedFilesNoted`); N13: the index-failure test matches Git's index refusals, not the word `index`, and the scope message no longer repeats itself; N14: a failed lookup keeps Git's cause and is not an index failure; N15: Git's message is kept on one bounded line and the report states it on one line; N16: `TestIndexFailuresAreNamedInAnyLocale`, `TestGitReadErrorsNameTheirCause` and `TestAFailedIndexHandOverIsAnIndexFailure` fail with each of those guards, the English locale, the context and the hand-over mark mutated out. A failing memfd write still has no test of its own (it falls back as a failing memfd does).\n+- 2026-11-26: review round 3 (rrn-bd7106fcc6ae8449) requested changes: the text classification missed index refusals and lost the cause behind a warning. Withdrawn for D3: `TestScopeSelectionTellsRevisionsFromIndexFailures` (a corrupt index behind a `diff.dirstat` warning is not an unknown revision; an unknown revision in a range is) fails with the resolution or the label mutated; `TestGitReadErrorsNameTheirCause` fails with the first-line cut restored; `TestIndexFailuresAreNamedInAnyLocale` fails with the absolute path kept. N19–N21 are follow-ups or answered by D3.\n \n ### Results summary\n The full `pose-mcp` suite passes; the canonical result is refreshed with `pose validate --carry`.\n \n ### Requirement trace\n - R1 [satisfied] test:TestReadOnlyIndexToleratesAnAtomicallyReplacedIndex, test:TestReadOnlyIndexRefusesAFIFOIndex\n-- R2 [satisfied] test:TestAFailedIndexReadIsReported, test:TestACorruptIndexIsReportedWithItsCause, test:TestIndexFailuresAreNamedInAnyLocale, test:TestGitReadErrorsNameTheirCause, test:TestAFailedIndexHandOverIsAnIndexFailure\n+- R2 [satisfied] test:TestScopeSelectionTellsRevisionsFromIndexFailures, test:TestAFailedIndexReadIsReported, test:TestACorruptIndexIsReportedWithItsCause, test:TestIndexFailuresAreNamedInAnyLocale, test:TestGitReadErrorsNameTheirCause, test:TestAFailedIndexHandOverIsAnIndexFailure\n - R3 [satisfied] test:TestReadOnlyIndexFindsTheIndexFromASubdirectory\n - R4 [satisfied] test:TestThePrivateIndexCopyLeavesTheIndexAlone, test:TestReadOnlyIndexFallsBackWithoutAMemoryFile\n - R5 [satisfied] (accepted limit L1, decision D1)\n@@ -156,4 +157,5 @@ L1 above.\n Origin: `pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone` (done 2026-11-26).\n - [open] Test the index lookup against a Git that echoes an unknown `--path-format` (a stand-in executable), so restoring the flag fails a test (review round 1, N6). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-26)\n - [open] Test the `pose report` warning for an unreadable change list end to end (review round 1, N7). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-26)\n+- [open] Add failing tests for the guards round 3 listed (the ledger passing its context, `GitEnglish` on the check, hand-over and lookup, the report's stderr warning, the memfd write fallback), and a locale test that does not depend on Git's pt_BR translations being installed (review rounds 2 N16, 3 N21). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-26)\n - [open] List the changed specs of a POSE root below the repository top: `git diff --name-only` names top-relative paths that the `.pose/specs/` filter drops, so their ready transitions go unchecked (review round 1, N11; pre-existing). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-12-26)\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\nindex 3456e3d2..0300649f 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\n@@ -298,7 +298,8 @@ func readLastReportRecord(path string) *reportRecord {\n }\n \n // reportChangedFilesNoted is reportChangedFiles for the report: outside a\n-// repository the plain listing stays silent, as before (review round 1, N9);\n+// repository Git can open at all the plain listing stays silent, as before\n+// (review round 1, N9; round 3, N19);\n // any other failure is returned to warn about and stated in the list, on\n // one line (review round 2, N12, N15).\n func reportChangedFilesNoted(root, since string, locale cliLocale) ([]string, error) {\n@@ -309,7 +310,12 @@ func reportChangedFilesNoted(root, since string, locale cliLocale) ([]string, er\n \tif since == \"\" && posemodel.RawGit(\"-C\", root, \"rev-parse\", \"--git-dir\").Run() != nil {\n \t\treturn files, nil\n \t}\n-\tnote := strings.ReplaceAll(err.Error(), \"\\n\", \" \")\n+\t// One line, bounded, without the checkout's absolute path, since the\n+\t// report is versioned (review round 3, N22).\n+\tnote := strings.ReplaceAll(strings.ReplaceAll(err.Error(), \"\\n\", \" \"), root, \"<root>\")\n+\tif len(note) > 600 {\n+\t\tnote = note[:600] + \"…\"\n+\t}\n \treturn []string{cliText(locale, \"_The changed files could not be listed: \", \"_Os arquivos alterados não puderam ser listados: \") + note + \"_\"}, err\n }\n \ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_reads_index_test.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_reads_index_test.go\nindex 272a7f08..369e0a34 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_reads_index_test.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_reads_index_test.go\n@@ -2,7 +2,6 @@ package cli\n \n import (\n \t\"bytes\"\n-\t\"errors\"\n \tposemodel \"github.com/harne8/pose-mcp/internal/pose\"\n \t\"os\"\n \t\"os/exec\"\n@@ -214,10 +213,10 @@ func TestIndexFailuresAreNamedInAnyLocale(t *testing.T) {\n \t\tt.Fatal(err)\n \t}\n \tfiles, err := reportChangedFilesNoted(root, \"\", localeEN)\n-\tif !errors.Is(err, posemodel.ErrIndexUnreadable) {\n-\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a corrupt index in another locale was not named: %v\", err)\n+\tif err == nil || !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"index file\") {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a corrupt index in another locale was not named in Git's English words: %v\", err)\n \t}\n-\tif len(files) != 1 || !strings.HasPrefix(files[0], \"_The changed files could not be listed: \") || strings.Contains(files[0], \"\\n\") {\n+\tif len(files) != 1 || !strings.HasPrefix(files[0], \"_The changed files could not be listed: \") || strings.Contains(files[0], \"\\n\") || strings.Contains(files[0], root) {\n \t\tt.Fatalf(\"the report did not state the failure on one line: %q\", files)\n \t}\n \tclean, _ := staleIndexRepo(t)\n@@ -229,4 +228,30 @@ func TestIndexFailuresAreNamedInAnyLocale(t *testing.T) {\n \tif files, err := reportChangedFilesNoted(outside, \"\", localeEN); err != nil || len(files) != 0 {\n \t\tt.Fatalf(\"a plain report outside a repository was not silent: %q %v\", files, err)\n \t}\n+\t// A failure naming the checkout reaches the versioned report without its\n+\t// absolute path (review round 3, N22).\n+\tif files, err := reportChangedFilesNoted(outside, \"HEAD\", localeEN); err == nil || len(files) != 1 || strings.Contains(files[0], outside) || !strings.Contains(files[0], \"<root>\") {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the report kept the checkout's path: %q %v\", files, err)\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+// Review round 3, N17–N18: a corrupt index is not taken for an unknown\n+// revision, whatever Git says first, and an unknown revision is found by\n+// resolving it.\n+func TestScopeSelectionTellsRevisionsFromIndexFailures(t *testing.T) {\n+\troot, _ := staleIndexRepo(t)\n+\tcmd := exec.Command(\"git\", \"-C\", root, \"config\", \"diff.dirstat\", \"bogus\")\n+\tif out, err := cmd.CombinedOutput(); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err, string(out))\n+\t}\n+\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(root, \".git\", \"index\"), []byte(\"not an index at all\"), 0o644); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\t_, err := computeChangedScopeWith(root, \"HEAD\", \"\", nil, scopeMetadata{})\n+\tif err == nil || strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"revision unknown?\") || !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"index file\") {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a corrupt index behind a configuration warning: %v\", err)\n+\t}\n+\tif _, err := computeChangedScopeWith(root, \"HEAD..nonexistent\", \"\", nil, scopeMetadata{}); err == nil || !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"revision unknown?\") {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"an unknown revision in a range: %v\", err)\n+\t}\n }\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\nindex 5cba94e5..6a1f4b13 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\n@@ -104,12 +104,17 @@ func computeChangedScopeWith(root, base, head string, modules []validationModule\n \tgitArgs = append(gitArgs, \"--\")\n \t// The diff reads the index without writing it (spec\n \t// pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone R1).\n-\tout, err := posemodel.RawGitDiffReadOnly(root, gitArgs...)\n-\tif errors.Is(err, posemodel.ErrIndexUnreadable) {\n-\t\treturn sel, fmt.Errorf(\"scope selection over %s: %v\", sel.rangeLabel(), err)\n+\t// A revision is judged by resolving it, not by reading Git's message\n+\t// (review rounds 2 N13, 3 N17–N18): only then is a failure \"revision\n+\t// unknown?\"; any other is reported with Git's own words.\n+\tfor _, rev := range scopeRevisions(base, head) {\n+\t\tif posemodel.RawGit(\"-C\", root, \"rev-parse\", \"--verify\", \"--quiet\", rev+\"^{commit}\").Run() != nil {\n+\t\t\treturn sel, fmt.Errorf(\"git diff %s failed (revision unknown?): %s does not name a commit\", sel.rangeLabel(), rev)\n+\t\t}\n \t}\n+\tout, err := posemodel.RawGitDiffReadOnly(root, gitArgs...)\n \tif err != nil {\n-\t\treturn sel, fmt.Errorf(\"git diff %s failed (revision unknown?): %v\", sel.rangeLabel(), err)\n+\t\treturn sel, fmt.Errorf(\"scope selection over %s: %v\", sel.rangeLabel(), err)\n \t}\n \tfor _, name := range strings.Split(string(out), \"\\x00\") {\n \t\tif name != \"\" {\n@@ -248,3 +253,25 @@ func declaredDependencyHits(file string, deps []string) []string {\n \t}\n \treturn hits\n }\n+\n+// scopeRevisions are the revisions a scope diff names: base and head, and the\n+// ends of a range written A..B or A...B.\n+func scopeRevisions(base, head string) []string {\n+\tvar revs []string\n+\tfor _, r := range []string{base, head} {\n+\t\tif r == \"\" {\n+\t\t\tcontinue\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tsep := \"..\"\n+\t\tif strings.Contains(r, \"...\") {\n+\t\t\tsep = \"...\"\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tfor _, part := range strings.Split(r, sep) {\n+\t\t\tif part == \"\" {\n+\t\t\t\tpart = \"HEAD\"\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\trevs = append(revs, part)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\treturn revs\n+}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go\nindex 2682101d..5bd7dc38 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go\n@@ -9,7 +9,6 @@ import (\n \t\"os\"\n \t\"os/exec\"\n \t\"path/filepath\"\n-\t\"regexp\"\n \t\"strings\"\n \t\"time\"\n )\n@@ -102,36 +101,27 @@ func ReadOnlyIndexContext(ctx context.Context, cmd *exec.Cmd, root string) (func\n \treturn done, nil\n }\n \n-// gitIndexFailureRE matches what Git says, in English, when it refuses the\n-// index itself (review round 2, N13: the word \"index\" alone also matched a\n-// revision named after it).\n-var gitIndexFailureRE = regexp.MustCompile(`(?i)\\bindex file\\b|\\bbad (index file )?signature\\b|\\bindex uses \\S+ extension\\b|\\bbad index version\\b`)\n-\n // gitReadSaidLimit bounds what a read error keeps of Git's standard error.\n-const gitReadSaidLimit = 300\n+const gitReadSaidLimit = 600\n \n-// GitReadError describes a failed git read with the first line of what git\n-// said on standard error, bounded, marking it ErrIndexUnreadable when git\n-// refused the index (review rounds 1 N1–N2, 2 N13, N15). Git must run with\n-// LC_ALL=C for the mark to hold in any locale.\n+// GitReadError describes a failed git read with what git said on standard\n+// error, all of it on one line and bounded, so a warning Git prints first\n+// does not hide the cause (review round 3, N17). It does not guess from the\n+// words whether the index was at fault: ErrIndexUnreadable marks only the\n+// failures of ReadOnlyIndex itself (review rounds 2 N13, 3 N18).\n func GitReadError(what string, err error, stderr []byte) error {\n-\tsaid := strings.TrimSpace(string(stderr))\n-\tif k := strings.IndexByte(said, '\\n'); k >= 0 {\n-\t\tsaid = strings.TrimSpace(said[:k])\n-\t}\n+\tsaid := strings.Join(strings.Fields(strings.ReplaceAll(string(stderr), \"\\n\", \" ; \")), \" \")\n \tif len(said) > gitReadSaidLimit {\n \t\tsaid = said[:gitReadSaidLimit] + \"…\"\n \t}\n \tif said == \"\" {\n \t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"%s failed: %w\", what, err)\n \t}\n-\tif gitIndexFailureRE.MatchString(said) {\n-\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"%s failed: %w: %w: %s\", what, ErrIndexUnreadable, err, said)\n-\t}\n \treturn fmt.Errorf(\"%s failed: %w: %s\", what, err, said)\n }\n \n-// GitEnglish makes cmd's messages English, so GitReadError can read them.\n+// GitEnglish makes cmd's messages English, so the causes reported read the\n+// same in every locale.\n func GitEnglish(cmd *exec.Cmd) {\n \tcmd.Env = append(cmd.Env, \"LC_ALL=C\", \"LANGUAGE=C\")\n }\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_test.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_test.go\nindex 09e497ec..2778ee05 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_test.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_test.go\n@@ -421,16 +421,15 @@ func TestReadOnlyIndexDiffCoversConflictsRangesAndDirtySubmodules(t *testing.T)\n // outside a repository is not an index failure, and the lookup honours the\n // caller's context.\n func TestGitReadErrorsNameTheirCause(t *testing.T) {\n-\tlong := \"fatal: index file smaller than expected \" + strings.Repeat(\"x\", 500) + \"\\nsecond line\"\n-\terr := GitReadError(\"git diff\", errors.New(\"exit status 128\"), []byte(long))\n-\tif !errors.Is(err, ErrIndexUnreadable) || strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"second line\") || len(err.Error()) > 400 {\n-\t\tt.Fatalf(\"an index refusal: %v\", err)\n-\t}\n-\tif err := GitReadError(\"git diff\", errors.New(\"exit status 128\"), []byte(\"fatal: index file corrupt\\nhint: second line\")); strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"second line\") {\n-\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a multi-line message was kept whole: %v\", err)\n-\t}\n-\tif err := GitReadError(\"git diff\", errors.New(\"exit status 128\"), []byte(\"fatal: bad revision 'feature/index-rework'\")); errors.Is(err, ErrIndexUnreadable) {\n-\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a revision named after the index: %v\", err)\n+\t// A warning first does not hide the cause; all of it is one line.\n+\terr := GitReadError(\"git diff\", errors.New(\"exit status 128\"), []byte(\"warning: Found errors in 'diff.dirstat' config variable:\\nfatal: index file corrupt\\n\"))\n+\tif !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"fatal: index file corrupt\") || strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"\\n\") {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the cause behind a warning: %q\", err)\n+\t}\n+\t// Bounded, and never classified from its words.\n+\terr = GitReadError(\"git diff\", errors.New(\"exit status 128\"), []byte(\"fatal: index file smaller than expected \"+strings.Repeat(\"x\", 2000)))\n+\tif len(err.Error()) > 700 || errors.Is(err, ErrIndexUnreadable) {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a long message: %d bytes, index-marked %v\", len(err.Error()), errors.Is(err, ErrIndexUnreadable))\n \t}\n \toutside := t.TempDir()\n \tt.Setenv(\"GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES\", filepath.Dir(outside))","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"945fc0d7-702e-46e1-a4f9-9fe916e2337c","timestamp":"2026-11-27T03:45:54.175Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"diff --git a/.pose/specs/2026-11-26-pose-validate-read-only-index-followups.md b/.pose/specs/2026-11-26-pose-validate-read-only-index-followups.md\nindex 626a8ed2..9143e637 100644\n--- a/.pose/specs/2026-11-26-pose-validate-read-only-index-followups.md\n+++ b/.pose/specs/2026-11-26-pose-validate-read-only-index-followups.md\n@@ -107,7 +107,7 @@ The index is judged on the file actually opened, opened with `O_NONBLOCK` where\n \n ### Decision D3\n - Basis: R2\n-The index lookup runs under the caller's context where the caller has one (`ReadOnlyIndexContext`, used by the review history reader within its 30 s), and under a 30 s bound of its own otherwise. Git's standard error is kept, as its first line within 300 bytes, and a failure in which Git refuses the index (`index file …`, `bad signature`, `index uses … extension`, `bad index version`) is marked `ErrIndexUnreadable`; every read whose error is classified runs with `LC_ALL=C` (`GitEnglish`), so that holds in any locale. A failed lookup of the index is reported with Git's words and is not an index failure (no repository, a broken config or HEAD). The report stays silent only where the root is not a repository.\n+The index lookup runs under the caller's context where the caller has one (`ReadOnlyIndexContext`, used by the review history reader within its 30 s), and under a 30 s bound of its own otherwise. A failure is never classified from Git's words, which two rounds showed incomplete in both directions (a revision named after the index, index refusals worded otherwise, a warning printed first): scope selection resolves its revisions first and says \"revision unknown?\" only when one does not name a commit, and reports any other failure with all of Git's standard error, on one line within 600 bytes, read with `LC_ALL=C`. `ErrIndexUnreadable` marks only the read-only index's own failures. The report stays silent only where Git cannot open the repository at all, and states any other failure on one line without the checkout's absolute path.\n \n ## 6. Validation\n \n@@ -123,13 +123,14 @@ Each requirement gets a regression test shown failing before its code.\n - 2026-11-26: R1 opens without blocking and judges the opened file; R2 reports a failed index read in `check`, names it in scope selection (`ErrIndexUnreadable`) and warns in `report`; R3 locates the index with `--git-path` relative to the root, within a 30 s deadline; R4 falls back to the private copy when the memory file or its time cannot be set. Each has a test that fails with its guard mutated out: `TestReadOnlyIndexToleratesAnAtomicallyReplacedIndex`, `TestAFailedIndexReadIsReported`, `TestReadOnlyIndexFindsTheIndexFromASubdirectory`, `TestThePrivateIndexCopyLeavesTheIndexAlone`. R6 adds `TestReadOnlyIndexDiffCoversConflictsRangesAndDirtySubmodules`, which passes on the existing reader. R5 is L1 (D1).\n - 2026-11-26: review round 1 (rrn-4262ae59adfc1641) requested changes. N1–N2: a corrupt index, which Git itself refuses, is now reported with Git's own message and marked as an index failure in check, scope selection and report (`TestACorruptIndexIsReportedWithItsCause`; fails with the classification or check's capture removed). N3: D3. N4: the memfd and timestamp calls are replaceable, and `TestReadOnlyIndexFallsBackWithoutAMemoryFile` fails with either fallback removed. N5: the R6 test makes the stat cache stale before every read, so it fails with the protection or the ledger's use of it removed, and the CLI concurrency test runs `ReviewRunHistoryFindings`. N8: failures handing the index to Git are index failures, and a failing memfd write falls back too. N9: the report states that the list could not be read, and a plain `pose report` outside a repository stays silent. N10: the check's findings are localised. N6, N7 and N11 are follow-ups.\n - 2026-11-26: review round 2 (rrn-ef7133259b2c911e) requested changes. N12: the plain `report` listing runs in English and is silent only outside a repository (`reportChangedFilesNoted`); N13: the index-failure test matches Git's index refusals, not the word `index`, and the scope message no longer repeats itself; N14: a failed lookup keeps Git's cause and is not an index failure; N15: Git's message is kept on one bounded line and the report states it on one line; N16: `TestIndexFailuresAreNamedInAnyLocale`, `TestGitReadErrorsNameTheirCause` and `TestAFailedIndexHandOverIsAnIndexFailure` fail with each of those guards, the English locale, the context and the hand-over mark mutated out. A failing memfd write still has no test of its own (it falls back as a failing memfd does).\n+- 2026-11-26: review round 3 (rrn-bd7106fcc6ae8449) requested changes: the text classification missed index refusals and lost the cause behind a warning. Withdrawn for D3: `TestScopeSelectionTellsRevisionsFromIndexFailures` (a corrupt index behind a `diff.dirstat` warning is not an unknown revision; an unknown revision in a range is) fails with the resolution or the label mutated; `TestGitReadErrorsNameTheirCause` fails with the first-line cut restored; `TestIndexFailuresAreNamedInAnyLocale` fails with the absolute path kept. N19–N21 are follow-ups or answered by D3.\n \n ### Results summary\n The full `pose-mcp` suite passes; the canonical result is refreshed with `pose validate --carry`.\n \n ### Requirement trace\n - R1 [satisfied] test:TestReadOnlyIndexToleratesAnAtomicallyReplacedIndex, test:TestReadOnlyIndexRefusesAFIFOIndex\n-- R2 [satisfied] test:TestAFailedIndexReadIsReported, test:TestACorruptIndexIsReportedWithItsCause, test:TestIndexFailuresAreNamedInAnyLocale, test:TestGitReadErrorsNameTheirCause, test:TestAFailedIndexHandOverIsAnIndexFailure\n+- R2 [satisfied] test:TestScopeSelectionTellsRevisionsFromIndexFailures, test:TestAFailedIndexReadIsReported, test:TestACorruptIndexIsReportedWithItsCause, test:TestIndexFailuresAreNamedInAnyLocale, test:TestGitReadErrorsNameTheirCause, test:TestAFailedIndexHandOverIsAnIndexFailure\n - R3 [satisfied] test:TestReadOnlyIndexFindsTheIndexFromASubdirectory\n - R4 [satisfied] test:TestThePrivateIndexCopyLeavesTheIndexAlone, test:TestReadOnlyIndexFallsBackWithoutAMemoryFile\n - R5 [satisfied] (accepted limit L1, decision D1)\n@@ -156,4 +157,5 @@ L1 above.\n Origin: `pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone` (done 2026-11-26).\n - [open] Test the index lookup against a Git that echoes an unknown `--path-format` (a stand-in executable), so restoring the flag fails a test (review round 1, N6). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-26)\n - [open] Test the `pose report` warning for an unreadable change list end to end (review round 1, N7). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-26)\n+- [open] Add failing tests for the guards round 3 listed (the ledger passing its context, `GitEnglish` on the check, hand-over and lookup, the report's stderr warning, the memfd write fallback), and a locale test that does not depend on Git's pt_BR translations being installed (review rounds 2 N16, 3 N21). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-26)\n - [open] List the changed specs of a POSE root below the repository top: `git diff --name-only` names top-relative paths that the `.pose/specs/` filter drops, so their ready transitions go unchecked (review round 1, N11; pre-existing). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-12-26)\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\nindex 3456e3d2..0300649f 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\n@@ -298,7 +298,8 @@ func readLastReportRecord(path string) *reportRecord {\n }\n \n // reportChangedFilesNoted is reportChangedFiles for the report: outside a\n-// repository the plain listing stays silent, as before (review round 1, N9);\n+// repository Git can open at all the plain listing stays silent, as before\n+// (review round 1, N9; round 3, N19);\n // any other failure is returned to warn about and stated in the list, on\n // one line (review round 2, N12, N15).\n func reportChangedFilesNoted(root, since string, locale cliLocale) ([]string, error) {\n@@ -309,7 +310,12 @@ func reportChangedFilesNoted(root, since string, locale cliLocale) ([]string, er\n \tif since == \"\" && posemodel.RawGit(\"-C\", root, \"rev-parse\", \"--git-dir\").Run() != nil {\n \t\treturn files, nil\n \t}\n-\tnote := strings.ReplaceAll(err.Error(), \"\\n\", \" \")\n+\t// One line, bounded, without the checkout's absolute path, since the\n+\t// report is versioned (review round 3, N22).\