{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FfDoeQGWfpCL7Dnd4wbcjx","type":"tool_result","content":"ok  \tgithub.com/harne8/pose-mcp/internal/cli\t0.006s\n```pose-draft\n{\n \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n \"findings\": [\n  {\"id\":\"N23\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\",\"line\":111,\"summary\":\"The new commit resolution refuses revisions that git diff accepts and scope selection answered before: a tree as base or head (the empty tree 4b825dc642cb6eb9a060e54bf8d69288fbee4904, used to select everything, or any tree id) and HEAD^-. Each now fails as '(revision unknown?): <rev> does not name a commit' while the plain diff succeeds. A read changed its answer outside any requirement or decision. Reproduced with overlay probes.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"N24\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\",\"line\":112,\"summary\":\"Any failure of the rev-parse is reported as an unknown revision and Git's standard error is discarded: with a broken .git/config, outside a repository, or on a dubious-ownership refusal, scope selection says only '(revision unknown?): HEAD does not name a commit'. The cause and Git's safe.directory remedy are gone; the previous round's code reported Git's fatal line. Contradicts R2 and D3 (the label only when a revision does not name a commit, any other failure with Git's standard error). Reproduced with overlay probes.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"N25\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go\",\"line\":115,\"summary\":\"The 600-byte bound keeps the start of Git's standard error, so warnings longer than that still hide the fatal line: a long diff.dirstat warning ahead of a corrupt index leaves no cause in scope selection or the report.\",\"action\":\"When truncating, keep the fatal and error lines or the tail.\",\"owner\":\"pose-mcp maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-31\"},\n  {\"id\":\"N26\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\",\"line\":315,\"summary\":\"Only the root string is replaced, so the versioned report still carries absolute paths when the index lies outside it: a POSE root below the repository top, or a linked worktree whose index is under the main .git/worktrees.\",\"action\":\"Also replace the Git directory, or write no path into the note, and test both layouts.\",\"owner\":\"pose-mcp maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-31\"},\n  {\"id\":\"N27\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\",\"line\":264,\"summary\":\"No test selects a healthy A..B or A...B range: removing the splitting in scopeRevisions, which would refuse every such range, leaves the focused tests green. The report note's bound is untested too.\",\"action\":\"Test both range forms with resolvable ends and the note's bound.\",\"owner\":\"pose-mcp maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-31\"}\n ],\n \"prior_findings\": [\n  {\"id\":\"R1-N6\",\"status\":\"not-fixed\",\"evidence\":\"Overlay mutation restoring --path-format=absolute leaves the focused tests green; open spec follow-up.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R1-N7\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"Removing the check's command-failure finding fails TestACorruptIndexIsReportedWithItsCause; replacing the report warning call stays green; open spec follow-up.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R1-N11\",\"status\":\"not-fixed\",\"evidence\":\"The ready-transition diff in check.go is unchanged in f9c29770..119d0702; pre-existing, open spec follow-up.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R2-N12\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"TestIndexFailuresAreNamedInAnyLocale passes under pt_BR and fails with GitEnglish emptied. A broken config or HEAD stays silent, which rewritten D3 now states (probe).\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R2-N13\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"gitIndexFailureRE and the word match are gone (git_worktree_reads.go:104-120); probes show an unknown revision labelled by resolution and no doubled prefix.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R2-N15\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"Removing the bound fails TestGitReadErrorsNameTheirCause and removing the root replacement fails TestIndexFailuresAreNamedInAnyLocale; absolute paths outside the root remain (N26).\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R2-N16\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"Context, report locale, hand-over mark and silence mutations fail tests; the ledger context, other locale sites, memfd write and warning stay green; open spec follow-up.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R3-N17\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"TestScopeSelectionTellsRevisionsFromIndexFailures and TestGitReadErrorsNameTheirCause fail with the first-line cut restored; a preface over 600 bytes still hides the cause (N25).\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R3-N18\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"No text classification remains; validate_scope.go:110-118 labels only a failed resolution, and the label mutation fails three tests, so index refusals however worded are reported as scope selection failures.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R3-N19\",\"status\":\"superseded\",\"evidence\":\"Rewritten D3 states the report is silent where Git cannot open the repository at all; the broken-config probe behaves so (report.go:310).\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R3-N20\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"Diff and lookup failures after resolution are no longer labelled and the prefix is single; repository failures are still labelled as unknown revisions, now without the cause (N24).\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R3-N21\",\"status\":\"not-fixed\",\"evidence\":\"The ledger context, check, hand-over and lookup locale, warning and memfd write mutations stay green; recorded as an open spec follow-up.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R3-N22\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"Probe: the root is replaced by <root>; a subdirectory root and a linked worktree still write absolute paths (N26).\"}\n ],\n \"sweep\": \"Read the round 4 diff (f9c29770..119d0702) and callers; ran the focused cli and pose tests twice under -race and go vet; probed by overlay: empty tree, tree id, HEAD^-, ancestors, two- and three-dot ranges, unknown revision, broken config, non-repository, dubious ownership, a long warning ahead of a corrupt index, subdirectory and linked-worktree report notes; ran 23 guard mutations including FIFO, fallbacks and index protection; ran the planned pose tools and both validate commands.\",\n \"criteria\": [\n  {\"id\":\"assumption-integrity\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N23\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-concurrency\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-contracts\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N23\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-input-errors\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N24\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-integration-impact\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/check-git-spawns-integration\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-observability\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N24\"},\n  {\"id\":\"compatibility\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N23\"},\n  {\"id\":\"correctness\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N23\"},\n  {\"id\":\"design-causality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-1c8a3d3c63eb7a6a\",\"rationale\":\"D2 removes the stat-then-open race and keeps FIFOs from blocking (both mutations fail tests); D1 and L1 rest on measured Git behaviour; rewritten D3 removes the cause of R3-N18 by not classifying from text. Its resolution step is too narrow and drops causes, recorded as N23 and N24. The sealed design assessment lists no structural deltas.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"documentation\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N24\"},\n  {\"id\":\"operability\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N24\"},\n  {\"id\":\"requirements\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N24\"},\n  {\"id\":\"scope\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/artifact-claim-boundary-integration\",\"rationale\":\"The 13 implementation files are the ones the spec lists, artifact-check strict exits 0, and the round stays within R2 and D3; the behaviour change it brings is recorded as N23.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"security\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/engine-reads-raw-history-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Revisions pass safeGitRevRE before reaching rev-parse and diff, so none can be an option; the open path stays non-blocking, judged by fstat and bounded; Git environment sanitised; private copy 0600 and removed. Residual local paths in the report are low (N26).\"},\n  {\"id\":\"solution-proportionality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Dropping the classifier and resolving revisions is small and removes speculative text matching. The choice is invalid where a diff accepts a non-commit or where resolution fails for another reason (N23, N24); running the resolution only after the diff fails, keeping its stderr, would be as small and change no successful answer.\"}\n ],\n \"tools\": [\n  {\"id\":\"artifact-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-validate-read-only-index-followups --strict\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"assess-design\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-1c8a3d3c63eb7a6a\",\"rationale\":\"Observed, no deltas.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"assess-discover\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\"},\n  {\"id\":\"assess-integrate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/engine-reads-raw-history-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Three HTTP consumer gaps reported, on endpoints this range does not touch.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"assess-tech-debt\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\"rationale\":\"Ran; the scan reports itself incomplete because two older specs could not be read.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"closeout-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"Needs the completed review.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"review-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"Needs the recorded attestation.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"suggest-review\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\"},\n  {\"id\":\"surface-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/engine-reads-raw-history-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0 with zero findings.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"validate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Rerun in the sandbox: exit 1, 236 steps, 224 pass, 11 fail, 1 timeout. The failed tests match sandbox limits (directory ownership by another user, denied network and delegation, runtime tests failing to start or timing out) or sit in files this range does not touch. Focused subject tests pass under -race. Relies on the sealed evidence.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"validate\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Rerun in the sandbox: exit 1, 233 steps, 221 pass, 11 fail, 1 timeout. The failed tests match sandbox limits (directory ownership by another user, denied network and delegation, runtime tests failing to start or timing out) or sit in files this range does not touch. Focused subject tests pass under -race. Relies on the sealed evidence.\"}\n ]\n}\n```\nDraft check: the conclusion step would accept this draft.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"e3834d7e-54f1-42bb-b475-c7e7961daf75","timestamp":"2026-11-27T04:22:25.454Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"ok  \tgithub.com/harne8/pose-mcp/internal/cli\t0.006s\n```pose-draft\n{\n \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n \"findings\": [\n  {\"id\":\"N23\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\",\"line\":111,\"summary\":\"The new commit resolution refuses revisions that git diff accepts and scope selection answered before: a tree as base or head (the empty tree 4b825dc642cb6eb9a060e54bf8d69288fbee4904, used to select everything, or any tree id) and HEAD^-. Each now fails as '(revision unknown?): <rev> does not name a commit' while the plain diff succeeds. A read changed its answer outside any requirement or decision. Reproduced with overlay probes.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"N24\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\",\"line\":112,\"summary\":\"Any failure of the rev-parse is reported as an unknown revision and Git's standard error is discarded: with a broken .git/config, outside a repository, or on a dubious-ownership refusal, scope selection says only '(revision unknown?): HEAD does not name a commit'. The cause and Git's safe.directory remedy are gone; the previous round's code reported Git's fatal line. Contradicts R2 and D3 (the label only when a revision does not name a commit, any other failure with Git's standard error). Reproduced with overlay probes.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"N25\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go\",\"line\":115,\"summary\":\"The 600-byte bound keeps the start of Git's standard error, so warnings longer than that still hide the fatal line: a long diff.dirstat warning ahead of a corrupt index leaves no cause in scope selection or the report.\",\"action\":\"When truncating, keep the fatal and error lines or the tail.\",\"owner\":\"pose-mcp maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-31\"},\n  {\"id\":\"N26\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\",\"line\":315,\"summary\":\"Only the root string is replaced, so the versioned report still carries absolute paths when the index lies outside it: a POSE root below the repository top, or a linked worktree whose index is under the main .git/worktrees.\",\"action\":\"Also replace the Git directory, or write no path into the note, and test both layouts.\",\"owner\":\"pose-mcp maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-31\"},\n  {\"id\":\"N27\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\",\"line\":264,\"summary\":\"No test selects a healthy A..B or A...B range: removing the splitting in scopeRevisions, which would refuse every such range, leaves the focused tests green. The report note's bound is untested too.\",\"action\":\"Test both range forms with resolvable ends and the note's bound.\",\"owner\":\"pose-mcp maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-31\"}\n ],\n \"prior_findings\": [\n  {\"id\":\"R1-N6\",\"status\":\"not-fixed\",\"evidence\":\"Overlay mutation restoring --path-format=absolute leaves the focused tests green; open spec follow-up.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R1-N7\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"Removing the check's command-failure finding fails TestACorruptIndexIsReportedWithItsCause; replacing the report warning call stays green; open spec follow-up.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R1-N11\",\"status\":\"not-fixed\",\"evidence\":\"The ready-transition diff in check.go is unchanged in f9c29770..119d0702; pre-existing, open spec follow-up.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R2-N12\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"TestIndexFailuresAreNamedInAnyLocale passes under pt_BR and fails with GitEnglish emptied. A broken config or HEAD stays silent, which rewritten D3 now states (probe).\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R2-N13\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"gitIndexFailureRE and the word match are gone (git_worktree_reads.go:104-120); probes show an unknown revision labelled by resolution and no doubled prefix.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R2-N15\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"Removing the bound fails TestGitReadErrorsNameTheirCause and removing the root replacement fails TestIndexFailuresAreNamedInAnyLocale; absolute paths outside the root remain (N26).\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R2-N16\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"Context, report locale, hand-over mark and silence mutations fail tests; the ledger context, other locale sites, memfd write and warning stay green; open spec follow-up.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R3-N17\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"TestScopeSelectionTellsRevisionsFromIndexFailures and TestGitReadErrorsNameTheirCause fail with the first-line cut restored; a preface over 600 bytes still hides the cause (N25).\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R3-N18\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"No text classification remains; validate_scope.go:110-118 labels only a failed resolution, and the label mutation fails three tests, so index refusals however worded are reported as scope selection failures.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R3-N19\",\"status\":\"superseded\",\"evidence\":\"Rewritten D3 states the report is silent where Git cannot open the repository at all; the broken-config probe behaves so (report.go:310).\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R3-N20\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"Diff and lookup failures after resolution are no longer labelled and the prefix is single; repository failures are still labelled as unknown revisions, now without the cause (N24).\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R3-N21\",\"status\":\"not-fixed\",\"evidence\":\"The ledger context, check, hand-over and lookup locale, warning and memfd write mutations stay green; recorded as an open spec follow-up.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R3-N22\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"Probe: the root is replaced by <root>; a subdirectory root and a linked worktree still write absolute paths (N26).\"}\n ],\n \"sweep\": \"Read the round 4 diff (f9c29770..119d0702) and callers; ran the focused cli and pose tests twice under -race and go vet; probed by overlay: empty tree, tree id, HEAD^-, ancestors, two- and three-dot ranges, unknown revision, broken config, non-repository, dubious ownership, a long warning ahead of a corrupt index, subdirectory and linked-worktree report notes; ran 23 guard mutations including FIFO, fallbacks and index protection; ran the planned pose tools and both validate commands.\",\n \"criteria\": [\n  {\"id\":\"assumption-integrity\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N23\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-concurrency\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-contracts\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N23\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-input-errors\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N24\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-integration-impact\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/check-git-spawns-integration\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-observability\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N24\"},\n  {\"id\":\"compatibility\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N23\"},\n  {\"id\":\"correctness\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N23\"},\n  {\"id\":\"design-causality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-1c8a3d3c63eb7a6a\",\"rationale\":\"D2 removes the stat-then-open race and keeps FIFOs from blocking (both mutations fail tests); D1 and L1 rest on measured Git behaviour; rewritten D3 removes the cause of R3-N18 by not classifying from text. Its resolution step is too narrow and drops causes, recorded as N23 and N24. The sealed design assessment lists no structural deltas.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"documentation\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N24\"},\n  {\"id\":\"operability\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N24\"},\n  {\"id\":\"requirements\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N24\"},\n  {\"id\":\"scope\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/artifact-claim-boundary-integration\",\"rationale\":\"The 13 implementation files are the ones the spec lists, artifact-check strict exits 0, and the round stays within R2 and D3; the behaviour change it brings is recorded as N23.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"security\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/engine-reads-raw-history-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Revisions pass safeGitRevRE before reaching rev-parse and diff, so none can be an option; the open path stays non-blocking, judged by fstat and bounded; Git environment sanitised; private copy 0600 and removed. Residual local paths in the report are low (N26).\"},\n  {\"id\":\"solution-proportionality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Dropping the classifier and resolving revisions is small and removes speculative text matching. The choice is invalid where a diff accepts a non-commit or where resolution fails for another reason (N23, N24); running the resolution only after the diff fails, keeping its stderr, would be as small and change no successful answer.\"}\n ],\n \"tools\": [\n  {\"id\":\"artifact-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-validate-read-only-index-followups --strict\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"assess-design\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-1c8a3d3c63eb7a6a\",\"rationale\":\"Observed, no deltas.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"assess-discover\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\"},\n  {\"id\":\"assess-integrate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/engine-reads-raw-history-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Three HTTP consumer gaps reported, on endpoints this range does not touch.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"assess-tech-debt\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\"rationale\":\"Ran; the scan reports itself incomplete because two older specs could not be read.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"closeout-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"Needs the completed review.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"review